  "description_short": "Italian-inspired waterfront café serving fresh pasta, artisan coffee, and light meals with lagoon views.",
  "description_long": "Tucked along the Knysna Waterfront, L'Opera brings Italian café culture to the water's edge with a relaxed, all-day menu that spans breakfast pastries and cappuccinos through to evening pasta and wine. The setting is casual and unpretentious—perfect for watching boats drift by while you tuck into a carbonara or a wood-fired pizza. Their coffee is consistently good, and the deli counter stocks Italian imports if you want to take home some dried pasta or olive oil.\n\nThe lagoon views are a big drawcard, especially if you snag a table on the outdoor terrace. It's equally suited to a solo morning coffee, a light lunch with friends, or a casual dinner after browsing the Waterfront shops. The vibe is easygoing, and the kitchen keeps things simple and unfussy—fresh ingredients, classic preparations, nothing overcomplicated. A reliable spot when you want something tasty without the fuss.",
